Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 13:12:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] stage 280/283: a fixed window over a growing tape, and the
 harm crowding actually does

283 ran the ladder: 91 -> 792 -> 4730 slots, a 52x growth with the mind
byte-identical at every rung. Precision sagged 0.796 -> 0.740 -> 0.664 and
cleared its floor. The return path did not: separation fell 0.96 -> 0.885
-> 0.610.

It failed from the side I did not predict. The rate on values taken from
elsewhere in the tape stayed at zero throughout - accidental
co-occurrence never became a problem - while the rate on the value the
corpus settled on fell to 0.616, even though mentions per address ROSE
from 2.4 to 5.1. The corroborating mention was not missing; the top-7
window lost it to slots that share the value's words. So the check is
exact now: a slot holding the whole value holds the value's rarest word,
so its posting list contains every such slot and no ranking is involved.
Reproduced both ways on a hand-built tape where 200 decoys sit ahead of
the address's own mentions.

The same fixed k reaches the exam itself - witness_recall 0.977 -> 0.747
with 5.05 slots per address against a mean candidate list of 4.0 - so
283 now reports k_covers_address, and a reader can see the teacher
counting votes it was never shown.

And crowding gets a second reading. Nearest-other cosine at tau or above
reached 0.345 of addresses, but proximity between keys is a warning, not
damage: fp_addresses also demands shared words, so keys may crowd without
merging. The damage is a slot filed under an address its own text never
names, which needs no labels to count, so foreign_member_rate is the gate
now and crowding stays beside it as the leading indicator.

